Z||000001||88formula||04-19-2001||08:10 PM||||What I remember from school about the proportioning valve is that it limits hydraulic pressure to the rear brakes so that the rear brakes don't or are less likely to lock up.  It’s kind of like a prehistoric anti lock brake system. I have never removed or even messed around with one before but my guess would be that more hydraulic pressure will reach the rear brakes and you may be able to lock up you tires now.<P>As a result of locking up your tires it may take your car longer to come to a stop depending on the road conditions and the kind of tires you have. <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||fiero56||04-19-2001||08:11 PM||||If those rears lock up first, don't forget about the major handling chance that will follow.||||reg||1
